{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/996280-one-world-of-darkness","id":996280,"title":"One World of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-31T14:52:43-07:00","id":996280,"title":"One World of Darkness","content":"My personal headcanon: there is ONE World of Darkness, but EIGHT perspectives on that world (nine if you count the Wan Kuei). Feel free to discuss if you like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T18:29:34-07:00","id":996378,"title":"","content":"My personal headcanon changes with chronicle, I see no need to bound myself to just one version of the setting.<br /> <br /> That aside, it is perfectly doable as a hack/headcanon. But if you try to take every official material ever released into account, then you're going for a really bad trip and an utter failure at the end. It simply can't be done without changing something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T00:35:20-07:00","id":996483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/996280-one-world-of-darkness#post996280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal headcanon: there is ONE World of Darkness, but EIGHT perspectives on that world (nine if you count the Wan Kuei). Feel free to discuss if you like.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 9? Even the games themselves have points of contradiction. Its like the different models in physics each work with the data presented but some clearly contradict eachother but evidence points to either being true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T04:50:08-07:00","id":996529,"title":"","content":"I agree. In cases where the rules or (more rarely) the fluff contradict each other, I choose which one I'm going to follow. For example, for a long time I held that the Changing Breeds were descended from the beastmen created by the Lunar Exalted during the Age of Sorrows. However, as new material found in W20: Changing Breeds and Shattered Dreams seems to irreconcilably contradict this theory, I got rid of it and instead made the W20 origin the &quot;official&quot; canon in my chronicle. Thanks for listening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T08:20:33-07:00","id":996602,"title":"","content":"The issue is subjective versus objective viewpoints. If none of the factions have an objective viewpoint, then you can just have to work within the subjective viewpoint of the faction you are dealing with. I would suggest, however, determining the 'most correct' faction for your own usage, so you have something to interpret everything by. I use WtA, large groups of people use VtM or MtA, fewer people use CtD or WtO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T09:49:53-07:00","id":996658,"title":"","content":"That's a good idea. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T14:28:55-07:00","id":996812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/996280-one-world-of-darkness?p=996483#post996483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">9? Even the games themselves have points of contradiction. Its like the different models in physics each work with the data presented but some clearly contradict each other but evidence points to either being true.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like quantum physics?<br /> <br /> As for gaming that way, I've run with groups that do it pretty often. The trick is to never let the players have all the answers and let them come to their own conclusions. Blending themes is the only hard part, I tend to favor the lovecraftian style otherworldly horror blend(it lets you keep the personal horror of vampire, apocalyptic action of werewolf, transhumanism of mage, nihilism of wraith, etc. all wrapped in a tight little bow)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T14:47:27-07:00","id":996822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/996280-one-world-of-darkness?p=996529#post996529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. In cases where the rules or (more rarely) the fluff contradict each other, I choose which one I'm going to follow. For example, for a long time I held that the Changing Breeds were descended from the beastmen created by the Lunar Exalted during the Age of Sorrows. However, as new material found in W20: Changing Breeds and Shattered Dreams seems to irreconcilably contradict this theory, I got rid of it and instead made the W20 origin the &quot;official&quot; canon in my chronicle. Thanks for listening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted had any canonical connections cut before the game came out (anything remaining is an artifact of an earlier production cycle), so it never actually served as a canonical prehistory to a single WoD. This is all discussed in a sidebar in the first edition storyteller's companion (that book that came with the screen, that also mentioned the Eye of Autochthon for the first time), which mentioned that they were just elseworlds versions of each other with different genres and moods in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T21:03:08-07:00","id":996990,"title":"","content":"Just a thought that occurred to me viewing a random episode of Gravity Falls, Weirdmageddon Part 1.<br /> <br /> What if the end of times actually created the One WoD? As each &quot;line&quot; (not necessarily gameline, but as much distinct versions of the setting the ST wants to use) comes to an end, the barriers between universes colapse, as do the very prophecies that created then. As beings of distinct universes travel, willingly or not, to a common ground, a patchwork universe is born from the &quot;ashes&quot; of what came before. In my thoughts it isn't necessarily a time of destruction, but of maddening weirdness and complete surprise, as Ancient vampires and the Hydra of Corruption both awaken to a world too incoherent for them to really seize in any meaningful way.<br /> <br /> It isn't a complete thing in my head, yet, but I think I'll work further on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T21:44:16-07:00","id":997003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/996280-one-world-of-darkness?p=996990#post996990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a thought that occurred to me viewing a random episode of Gravity Falls, Weirdmageddon Part 1.<br /> <br /> What if the end of times actually created the One WoD? As each &quot;line&quot; (not necessarily gameline, but as much distinct versions of the setting the ST wants to use) comes to an end, the barriers between universes colapse, as do the very prophecies that created then. As beings of distinct universes travel, willingly or not, to a common ground, a patchwork universe is born from the &quot;ashes&quot; of what came before. In my thoughts it isn't necessarily a time of destruction, but of maddening weirdness and complete surprise, as Ancient vampires and the Hydra of Corruption both awaken to a world too incoherent for them to really seize in any meaningful way.<br /> <br /> It isn't a complete thing in my head, yet, but I think I'll work further on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think would be a better explanation than we are likely to get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T05:33:21-07:00","id":997093,"title":"","content":"Saur Ops Specialist: I am aware that Exalted is not officially the prehistory of the World of Darkness; you have pointed this out to me in previous posts. However, to the extent that this is not DIRECTLY contradicted by an entire sourcebook (as happened with Shattered Dreams), I try as best as possible to merge Exalted and WoD into one coherent timeline. This is not to suggest that my version is in any way canon; this is strictly for my timeline and my chronicles. I know there is no official connection; I just create one anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T08:45:40-07:00","id":997164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/996280-one-world-of-darkness?p=996990#post996990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a thought that occurred to me viewing a random episode of Gravity Falls, Weirdmageddon Part 1.<br /> <br /> What if the end of times actually created the One WoD? As each &amp;quot;line&amp;quot; (not necessarily gameline, but as much distinct versions of the setting the ST wants to use) comes to an end, the barriers between universes colapse, as do the very prophecies that created then. As beings of distinct universes travel, willingly or not, to a common ground, a patchwork universe is born from the &amp;quot;ashes&amp;quot; of what came before. In my thoughts it isn't necessarily a time of destruction, but of maddening weirdness and complete surprise, as Ancient vampires and the Hydra of Corruption both awaken to a world too incoherent for them to really seize in any meaningful way.<br /> <br /> It isn't a complete thing in my head, yet, but I think I'll work further on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of like the later books in The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy series where, once destroyed, Earths from alternate universes plop into the place of the missing one because it exists in a faultline in reality. As a result, there are multiple versions of some of the characters running around and The Guide Mark II is created as a pandimensional bridge to destroy all versions of Earth in all realities.<br /> <br /> In this One World of Darkness, the fragments of disparate conflicting and overlapping universes might fold in on themselves to create a new one in the space left by the absence of a world in the primary universe (primary from the PCs' perspective, of course) after the End Times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T09:21:38-07:00","id":997190,"title":"","content":"I'm even thinking about a villain that no one expected, one part Guide Mark II, other part Bill Cipher. But I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> Either way, the core idea is for the folding of realities be the End Times itself. As the worlds end, they also clash and mix. The event was prophecied, but it will make all prophecies null and altogether irrelevant once it starts properly. Maybe the PCs aren't even from the same original dimension, specially (but not only) if it is a crossover game. The utterly strange becomes the order of the day while the Powers Who Waited To End The World are simply as clueless of what's going on as everyone else.<br /> <br /> This odd apocalypse somehow end with a restructuring of reality at the ST's taste. Maybe the new world is fully aware of what happened. Maybe no one can remember. But what will make it truly interesting for a One WoD is to get rid of the very necessity of coherence with the past. Somehow it is clear for the supernatural creatures that things changed, and if remnants of their worlds and several more can be as ancient as ever, actually no one can truly know this &quot;New World of Darkness&quot;.<br /> <br /> By the way, if I do this thing, I'll probably adapt the game to CoD 2nd's system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T10:42:45-07:00","id":997234,"title":"","content":"I could see Exalted being the prehistory of CoD, but not WoD. Within CoD, you have predatory Fae, you do not have a prehistoric memory that goes back a quarter of a billion years, and you have a lot of minor supernatural creatures that could have been created during the end of the Second Age (especially with Exalted 3e, sorcery workings are more than flexible enough to create every form of supernatural creature that still exists in CoD).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:41:09-07:00","id":997275,"title":"","content":"Interesting idea. Thanks, Aya Tari.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:53:49-07:00","id":997288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/996280-one-world-of-darkness?p=997093#post997093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saur Ops Specialist: I am aware that Exalted is not officially the prehistory of the World of Darkness; you have pointed this out to me in previous posts. However, to the extent that this is not DIRECTLY contradicted by an entire sourcebook (as happened with Shattered Dreams), I try as best as possible to merge Exalted and WoD into one coherent timeline. This is not to suggest that my version is in any way canon; this is strictly for my timeline and my chronicles. I know there is no official connection; I just create one anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 1e STC was a pretty big contradiction. As was the subsequent development of Exalted, culminating in the Sidereals averting the transformation of Creation into any given WoD because they killed the Solars and brought about the Usurpation, thus doing something instead of sitting on their thumbs and allowing the name-dropped <u><b>WORLD OF DARKNESS!</b></u> to occur from their inaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T14:29:54-07:00","id":997374,"title":"","content":"Let me explain what I mean by a big contradiction. If I hadn't changed my history to accommodate it, the entire Shattered Dreams sourcebook would be useless to me. By contrast, the example you cite is one paragraph in the Sidereals book which can easily be ignored or glossed over. Furthermore, Exalted was advertised very, very heavily as being the prehistory of the World of Darkness, and the only reason I bought it was because I thought it was a WoD prehistory game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T15:29:45-07:00","id":997405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/996280-one-world-of-darkness?p=997190#post997190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm even thinking about a villain that no one expected, one part Guide Mark II, other part Bill Cipher. But I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> Either way, the core idea is for the folding of realities be the End Times itself. As the worlds end, they also clash and mix. The event was prophecied, but it will make all prophecies null and altogether irrelevant once it starts properly. Maybe the PCs aren't even from the same original dimension, specially (but not only) if it is a crossover game. The utterly strange becomes the order of the day while the Powers Who Waited To End The World are simply as clueless of what's going on as everyone else.<br /> <br /> This odd apocalypse somehow end with a restructuring of reality at the ST's taste. Maybe the new world is fully aware of what happened. Maybe no one can remember. But what will make it truly interesting for a One WoD is to get rid of the very necessity of coherence with the past. Somehow it is clear for the supernatural creatures that things changed, and if remnants of their worlds and several more can be as ancient as ever, actually no one can truly know this &amp;quot;New World of Darkness&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> By the way, if I do this thing, I'll probably adapt the game to CoD 2nd's system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this idea very much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T17:50:05-07:00","id":997464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/996280-one-world-of-darkness?p=997374#post997374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me explain what I mean by a big contradiction. If I hadn't changed my history to accommodate it, the entire Shattered Dreams sourcebook would be useless to me. By contrast, the example you cite is one paragraph in the Sidereals book which can easily be ignored or glossed over. Furthermore, Exalted was advertised very, very heavily as being the prehistory of the World of Darkness, and the only reason I bought it was because I thought it was a WoD prehistory game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Advertised as, and then promptly retconned out before release date to be its own thing. Thankfully, we didn't end up with an Earthdawn and Shadowrun situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T18:18:05-07:00","id":997480,"title":"","content":"Hence the term &quot;false advertising.&quot; And I happen to like Earthdawn and Shadowrun for exactly that reason. Don't assume that Exalted &quot;being its own thing&quot; is necessarily a good thing. Exalted should have tied into the World of Darkness a lot more closely than it did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T18:35:18-07:00","id":997489,"title":"","content":"I don't think Exalted should have tied into the World of Darkness. It would rob both games of the possibilities of independent development.<br /> <br /> But I'm not against incorporating it as an option, either.<br /> <br /> Actually, you two contending over the issue seems kind of silly. Just present your opinions on the One World, be it with or without Exalted. Just present your takes on this and the benefits you see in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T20:14:35-07:00","id":997526,"title":"","content":"The Creation of Exalted could exist beyond the Deep Dreaming of the Changeling, the point where dreams unravel into Pure Chaos, and could be concurrent with cWoD. While the 'physics' of Exalted would not fly outside of that region, Creation could have been formed with the metaphysics of the Material Plane as a model by the Primordials. While Exalted physics might not translate to the Material Plane, cWoD might translate to Creation, allowing some fascinating crossover potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T23:26:45-07:00","id":997572,"title":"","content":"Eh there are debates in all fields about physics, history, biology where new discoveries are requiring revised views on reality. There are regularly competing theories of such that work with limited aspects of data that don't work on a broader level when you bring in more stuff, but they seem to work well in theirown corner. That the World of Darkness has this level of confusion and arguments is perhaps the most realistic aspect of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T04:16:43-07:00","id":997626,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry. As a girl who loves drama, sometimes I exaggerate my arguments for dramatic effect. I actually own a number of Second Edition Exalted books, and I think it's a great game on its own merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T20:24:52-07:00","id":998046,"title":"","content":"I preferred the First Edition myself, as I have the complete collection, though a few of my books are falling apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T05:35:31-07:00","id":998188,"title":"","content":"Aya Tari: Do you have First Edition Exalted? If so, is there a reference to Caine in there, or is that just a rumor? Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T05:36:03-07:00","id":998189,"title":"","content":"Sorry, meant to say First Edition Abyssals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T08:08:23-07:00","id":998228,"title":"","content":"I do, and I do not know. I took a look, but I did not find a mention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T10:41:42-07:00","id":998304,"title":"","content":"Aya Tari: Thank you! If someone who knows Exalted as well as you doesn't know about it, it's probably just a rumor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T18:33:36-07:00","id":998541,"title":"","content":"You are welcome. It could have always been in the first draft, but Abyssal was created when they started changing their mind about the WoD connection to Creation. I like to think that it is a concurrent world, like Scion or Aberrant, rather than prehistory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T19:13:33-07:00","id":998561,"title":"","content":"I always though the 13 Deathlords matching clans was a closer easter Egg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T19:52:21-07:00","id":998579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/996280-one-world-of-darkness?p=998561#post998561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always though the 13 Deathlords matching clans was a closer easter Egg.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then again, four of the Deathlords are left undescribed, and the earlier design phases (to which EX3 has actually reverted, since every doom imminent and backed by super-powered elders was cramping a lot of the setting's other features) had the potential for many, many more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T08:44:23-07:00","id":998781,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it was just a reflection of WW obsession with the number 13 in cWoD, which evolved into an obsession with the number 5 by nWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T18:52:53-07:00","id":998988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/996280-one-world-of-darkness?p=998781#post998781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it was just a reflection of WW obsession with the number 13 in cWoD, which evolved into an obsession with the number 5 by nWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Both have strong mystic symbolism. just if I were going to try and connect Abyssals to kindred I'd match Deathlords to Clans","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T14:50:04-08:00","id":1000997,"title":"","content":"In my version, Caine was a barbarian from beyond Creation who was cursed by God (an aspect of the Unconquered Sun) to become the first vampire. This is entirely my own head canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}